* SIMULATE core deck - fz parametric SKELETON (SIMULATE-3 card style).
* Complete the core description (loading map, library, geometry) with the decks
* of your own methodology; only the fz parameterization is illustrated here.
* fz parameters use the dollar-brace syntax, with a default value after "~".
'COM' fz parametric core calculation /
'TIT.CAS' 'fz-demo' /
* Nuclear data library produced by CMS-LINK (ship it with the input or use
* fzr --input_static, or give an absolute path)
'LIB' 'cms.lib' /
* Core thermal power and flow (% of nominal)
'PWR' ${core_power~100.0} /
'FLO' ${core_flow~100.0} /
* Initial boron guess (ppm)
'BOR' ${boron_guess~1200} /
* Cycle depletion: exposure steps (GWd/t) up to the cycle length
'DEP.CYC' 'CYCLE1' 0.0 1 /
'DEP.STA' 'AVE' 0.0 0.15 0.5 -1 ${cycle_length~18.0} /
'STA' /
'END' /
